{"groups":[{"members":["c1"],"primary":"c1","title":"San Francisco Rent Ordinance just cause eviction requirements","requirement":"A landlord may evict a tenant from a unit covered by the Rent Ordinance only for one of the 17 just causes listed in Section 37.9(a), and that cause must be the dominant motive for the eviction. A just cause is also required to remove housing services such as garage, parking, storage and laundry.","key_value":"17 just cause reasons under Section 37.9(a)","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9(a)","coverage_conditions":"Rental units covered by the Rent Ordinance. Some tenancies exempt from the rent increase limits remain subject to the just cause provisions. These include units whose first Certificate of Occupancy was issued after June 13, 1979, tenancies eligible for a rent increase under Costa-Hawkins, and some tenancies whose rent is regulated by another government agency.","exemptions":"Expiration of a rental agreement or a change in ownership is not just cause. Landlords that comply with Section 37.2(r) may temporarily remove housing services for mandatory soft-story seismic retrofit work.","coverage_from":"c1","conflict_note":null},{"members":["c2","c3"],"primary":"c2","title":"San Francisco Rent Ordinance relocation payments for no-fault evictions (Section 37.9C)","requirement":"Landlords must pay relocation payments for evictions based on owner or relative move-in, demolition or permanent removal of a unit from housing use, temporary capital improvement work, or substantial rehabilitation. Payment amounts are set by effective period.","key_value":"Most recent archived period (3/01/24 – 2/28/25): $7,912.00 / $23,733.00 / $5,275.00 (first table) and $10,660.89 / $31,982.66 / $7,142.95 (second table). The source text does not give column labels, and these figures may not be current as of 2026-10-01.","status":"in_force","effective_date":null,"end_date":null,"citation":"S.F. Admin. Code § 37.9C","coverage_conditions":null,"exemptions":"Relocation payments for temporary capital improvement evictions of less than 20 days are governed by Cal. Civ. Code § 1947.9, not by Rent Ordinance § 37.9C.","coverage_from":"c3","conflict_note":null}],"dropped":[]}
